{
 "_about": "Reviewed by a person, read by scripts/fetch-place-photos.py. <country>: place id -> the English Wikipedia article that is that place's own (a redirect counts only when the target's lead image shows that exact place). no_article: places with no English Wikipedia article of their own (stay clusters, practical cards, rentals, fuel, street-food runs, and sights en.wikipedia does not cover), so they keep no photo rather than a nearby subject's. rejected: the place has an article but its lead image cannot be used (none, a map, another subject, or looked at and refused), with the reason, so a rerun never restores it. replaced: places whose article lead image was installed and later swapped for a better Commons file of the same place, with the file and the reason. A swapped photo gets a new file name (-v2) so the media cache, which keys photos by URL and keeps them across releases, drops the old one.",
